HST Office: adaptive AutoRecovery interval (owner decision 2026-11-13).

- officecfg Recovery.xcs: new AutoSave/HstLargeDocumentSize (MB, default 5, 0 = off) and
  AutoSave/HstLargeDocumentTimeIntervall (minutes, default 10). The 3-minute TimeIntervall stays in
  extensions/hst-vietnamese-tools/RecoveryDefaults.xcu.
- framework autorecovery.cxx: the global timer still follows TimeIntervall, and each document is
  due once it has been modified for its own interval (upstream getModifiedStateDuration logic). A
  document whose last known size exceeds HstLargeDocumentSize waits
  max(TimeIntervall, HstLargeDocumentTimeIntervall) instead, so large files do not stall the user
  every 3 minutes. The size is the larger of the local document file and its newest recovery
  backup, refreshed on load, after a user save and after every recovery save; a never-saved
  document counts as small until its first backup exists. Remote files are not inspected.
  Emergency and session saves skip the interval check as upstream, so large documents are still
  saved on crash and shutdown.
- cui optsavepage.ui + vi messages.po: tooltip on the interval field explains the large-document rule.

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).
Test: tests/unit/test_adaptive_autorecovery_patch.py.
